## The highlights query for Helix {Tangle}[editors/helix/queries/loom/highlights.scm]

Helix reads its queries from its own runtime directory, so a Helix setup copies this file there in place of the shared highlights. It differs from them only in the colour of a key.

=>

::[The frontmatter's colours]

::[A key in Helix]

::[Heading colours]

::[Specifiers and sinks]

::[Arrows and tildes]

::[Anchors]

::[Warps]

::[Notes]

## The injections query for Helix {Tangle}[editors/helix/queries/loom/injections.scm]

Helix's copy of the injections shares the rules that work by a file's name, and takes its own form of the two that read a language's name.

=>

::[Prose is Markdown]

::[Names Helix knows in lower case]

::[Named by a sink]

::[Named by the Package file]

::[A Prose section is Markdown]
